To establish TC adsorption–desorption equilibrium on the Ce-MOF photocatalyst, the dispersion was left at dark environment for 60 min. During the photocatalytic degradation experiment, up to 3 mL of the reaction mixture were extracted, centrifuged and filtered using a syringe filter (pore size < 0.22 μm) to eliminate Ce-MOF particles in the solution. The samples were subsequently analyzed using a UV–Vis spectrophotometer to determine their TC concentration. The removal efficiency was calculated using Eq. (1).1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
