XRD pattern of the Ce-MOF samples is shown in Fig. 4b. XRD spectra of Ce-MOF from literature are also demonstrated in Fig. 4b, which exhibits peaks at 2θ = 9.1°, 14.5° 15.3°, 18.2°, 28.2° 29.3° and 30.0°62. The XRD pattern of all samples reveal a high level of crystallinity. Analysis of the crystalline structure of Ce-MOFs suggests that the central Ce atom is coordinated by three oxygen atoms from ligand carboxylate groups and five oxygen atoms from water molecules as schematically depicted in Fig. 1b. The carboxylate groups of the ligand are identified as unidentate55. Furthermore, the crystallite sizes of the samples were calculated using the main XRD peaks and the Scherrer equation (Eq. 3) via Xpert HighScore Plus software64.3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
