				\begin{document}$$D = \frac{K\lambda }{{\beta \cos \theta }}$$\end{document}D=KλβcosθIn Eq. 3, D is the average size of crystallites, K is shape factor (dimensionless, typically ~ 0.9), λ is X-ray wavelength, β is full width at half maximum (FWHM) of the diffraction peak in radian, and θ is Bragg angle. Average size of Ce-MOF crystallites synthesized by SC, HT, and RT methods were 40 nm, 47 nm, and 48 nm, respectively.Figure 4
(a) FTIR spectra of Ce-MOFs synthesized by HT, RT, and SC methods, reference and terephthalic acid56; (b) XRD pattern of Ce-MOF synthesized by HT, RT, and SC methods and XRD pattern of Ce-MOF in reference62.

The band gap of Ce-MOF was measured using a spectrophotometric device in direct mode based on the Tauc plot method in which αhν is plotted vs. hν. According to Eq. 44\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
